00:26:31,990 --> 00:26:37,600
So now, we've got that K1 value
and then how it ends up looking.

489
00:26:37,600 --> 00:26:41,400
And that's really nice
because, again, it shows you,

490
00:26:41,400 --> 00:26:46,560
is this value that you're
returning one that you expected?

491
00:26:46,560 --> 00:26:49,210
And so now, we can come in here.

492
00:26:49,210 --> 00:26:51,630
We can hit Control-A again.

493
00:26:51,630 --> 00:26:55,500
And we can add our
sorting filter.

494
00:26:55,500 --> 00:27:01,700
And so now, we can call
this percent of total.

495
00:27:01,700 --> 00:27:04,790
And now if we sort by
largest to smallest,

496
00:27:04,790 --> 00:27:07,400
now we can say, OK, this
one campaign made up

497
00:27:07,400 --> 00:27:10,370
4% of our totals.

498
00:27:10,370 --> 00:27:13,350
And then if we do
like a running total--

499
00:27:13,350 --> 00:27:16,550
we're just going to do this
plus our current one, which

500
00:27:16,550 --> 00:27:18,425
for the first one isn't
going to do anything.

501
00:27:24,010 --> 00:27:30,923
It's Control-Z because I want
to do the previous value.

502
00:27:35,780 --> 00:27:41,210
So now, I can see
that actually only--

503
00:27:41,210 --> 00:27:42,175
let's come down here--

504
00:27:45,260 --> 00:27:51,920
only seven of my campaigns
make up about 25%

505
00:27:51,920 --> 00:27:55,050
of my overall
campaigns out of 50.

506
00:27:55,050 --> 00:27:57,390
And so that can help
us, again, start

507
00:27:57,390 --> 00:28:00,630
to evaluate are these
campaigns that we're pouring

508
00:28:00,630 --> 00:28:04,470
so much money in worth it?

509
00:28:04,470 --> 00:28:07,890
So that's just really a
taste of the different things

510
00:28:07,890 --> 00:28:09,490
that we're doing this week.

511
00:28:09,490 --> 00:28:12,010
I would recommend going
to your practice problems.

512
00:28:12,010 --> 00:28:20,110
And as a new summary
statistic pops up,

513
00:28:20,110 --> 00:28:21,940
watch the video related to that.

514
00:28:21,940 --> 00:28:25,710
We can count, we
can add, we can--

515
00:28:25,710 --> 00:28:27,680
all of these different things.

516
00:28:27,680 --> 00:28:30,390
Continue to read the textbook
and watch those videos

517
00:28:30,390 --> 00:28:32,800
as you're working through
your practice problems.

518
00:28:32,800 --> 00:28:34,890
And if you have any
questions, remember

519
00:28:34,890 --> 00:28:39,630
there is that Q&A thread on this
week's module that you can--

520
00:28:39,630 --> 00:28:42,280
I'm more than happy to
answer your questions there,

521
00:28:42,280 --> 00:28:44,850
or you're welcome to schedule
a time to meet with me,

522
00:28:44,850 --> 00:28:49,150
or pop into Friday
office hour at noon.

523
00:28:49,150 --> 00:28:52,070
Thanks, and good
luck with Excel.